          "Engage the Asian professional constituency with specificity on education policy, immigration and family reunification, economic opportunity in professional fields, and whether government is serving their advancement — this 25.52% of the district is evaluating whether you represent their interests, not inheriting partisan loyalty from their parents.",
          "Understand the 49% opposition as a professional-class realignment, not a temporary aberration: college-educated professionals in high-income suburbs are actively reconsidering party affiliation based on competence, institutional effectiveness, and alignment with their values — any candidate who treats 51% as a stable base rather than a fragile plurality will find it further eroded.",
          "Do not cede education policy or school governance to Democratic framing; in a district with 66.9% college-educated adults and median age 44.3, parents and professionals are directly invested in school quality, curriculum, and how schools function — this is your constituency's material concern, not a Democratic issue."
