          "Engage the district's small but meaningful communities of color — 14.63% Asian, 14.04% Hispanic, 3.11% Black — with constituent attention to their specific economic and civic concerns rather than token acknowledgment; these communities have economic stakes in the district and are not monolithic in their political orientation.",
          "Do not treat 64% as a durable floor: in an affluent, educated district with strong Democratic infrastructure in New York State, a challenger who better articulates why Republican governance serves this constituency's economic interests — or who successfully argues that Democratic policy offers superior returns on the issues that matter most to professionals — can move this seat toward genuine competitiveness."
