          "Address the renter-majority economic security agenda directly: at 50.3% renters in a $100K median income district, housing affordability and anti-displacement are urgent material concerns for a substantial constituency whose political participation is conditional on demonstrating that government is actively working to preserve their ability to stay in the community.",
          "Consolidate the homeowner majority on quality-of-life governance: school funding, property tax fairness, and neighborhood character are the material concerns of the asset-holding majority, but present these within a framework of shared community investment — not as zero-sum competition with renter economic security or minority community needs.",
          "Treat the 59% margin as dependent on sustained engagement with each major constituency: the 41% opposition is substantial enough that any divergence in turnout or preference among Asian, Latino, or renter voters is sufficient to change the outcome — this is a district that requires active maintenance, not one where incumbency automatically holds."
