          { name: "Over-Reliance on Partisan Messaging in a Non-Partisan Evaluation District", tag: "avoid", why: "NY-AD-36 is demographically and economically positioned to evaluate representatives on concrete service delivery — housing affordability, transit access, responsive constituent relations, neighborhood safety — rather than partisan talking points. A constituency with 55.8% college education, $94,667 income, and 84.3% renters has sophisticated expectations about what government can and should do, and they benchmark representation against visible progress on stated priorities. A representative who relies on generic Democratic messaging while housing affordability stalls, transit service remains poor, or constituent service is slow will find that messaging insufficient to hold support if a challenger offers concrete solutions. In a district this affluent and educated, citizens can distinguish between partisan rhetoric and actual governance delivery." }
