          "Understand that unopposed victory masks underlying competitive risk: a 55.8% college-educated, 35.7 median age, renter-majority constituency evaluates on governance competence and material improvement in quality of life — not partisan identity — and a credible challenger offering solutions on housing and transit would have real opening.",
          "Translate income level into constituent expectations: at $94,667 median income, this is an affluent district expecting professional-quality government services, responsive constituent relations, and demonstrable progress on stated priorities — falling short on these dimensions in an unopposed race creates vulnerability that becomes apparent only when serious opposition emerges."
