          "Engage Asian-plurality communities with ethnic and linguistic specificity: Korean, Chinese, Indian, Filipino, and other Asian residents have distinct immigration histories and governance expectations—generic multicultural messaging alienates rather than motivates; active community engagement in neighborhood languages and through ethnic media and organizations is the baseline for holding this district.",
          "Address public safety and school quality directly: these are the two issues most likely to drive Asian and Hispanic working-class voters toward Republican candidates if Democrats are perceived as weak or dismissive; concrete policing, school performance data, and investment in both are the deliverables that hold this district.",
          "Do not treat 55% as a safe majority: at 45% Republican in a district with cost-pressured renters and a mixed educational profile, the opposition is substantial and growing if Kim's governance record on housing, schools, or public safety is perceived as failing—this is a seat that requires active constituent engagement and demonstrated delivery, not confidence that Democratic registration will hold the margin."
