          "Engage the multiracial coalition actively: the 56.52% Black, 25.25% white, and 11.33% Hispanic composition requires that constituent service and policy leadership speak to specific concerns across these communities—equitable policing, economic mobility, neighborhood investment—rather than treating the Black Democratic plurality as the sole political focus.",
          "Build public safety legitimacy with specificity: younger renters and parents evaluate on whether neighborhoods are safe and whether policing is accountable; this is not a messaging issue but a governance obligation that requires visible investment in both community safety and police accountability mechanisms.",
          "Treat the unopposed 2024 win as a strategic warning, not a secure foundation: absent Republican investment, Democratic dominance looks complete; when a credible challenger appears, the seat will be determined by whether constituents believe Cunningham is delivering on housing, safety, and economic opportunity—not by partisan loyalty."
