          "Lead on the material concerns of young, high-income urban professionals: housing affordability and rental cost escalation despite $181k median income, small-business regulatory burden for the self-employed and entrepreneurs concentrated in this district, and quality-of-life service delivery (transit, sanitation, public safety) that directly affects daily life in a dense urban environment.",
          "Recognize the 61.9% renter rate as a coalition pressure point — renters' concerns about cost of living, tenant protections, and housing supply differ materially from homeowner priorities, and a 94% incumbent should actively engage this constituency's distinct needs rather than assuming renters are part of a unified 'urban progressive' coalition.",
