          { name: "Generic Partisan Messaging Without Specific Material Policy Answers", tag: "avoid", why: "In a working-class renter district with limited college attainment and median income below state averages, broad progressive positioning without specific answers to housing stability, tenant rights, healthcare access, and wage policy will register as abstract rather than responsive. A challenger who can articulate concrete policy solutions to the material constraints that organize working-class renter life — housing costs, healthcare barriers, wage stagnation — will find that generic messaging is insufficient insulation against the challenge." }
