          "Address job quality and wage progression directly: the 22.5% college attainment rate and sub-median income describe a working population whose economic mobility depends on wage growth in jobs that do not require four-year credentials — retail, service, healthcare support, transportation, and skilled trades are the actual employment landscape, and legislative focus on these sectors' job quality and advancement pathways is more relevant than abstract small-business incentives.",
          "Build visible constituent service infrastructure for working renters: childcare affordability, healthcare access for uninsured and underinsured households, transit reliability, and emergency financial assistance programs are the governing tools that build trust and credibility with a 34.7-year-old working population — not symbolic representation on advisory boards.",
          "Recognize that 92% is not a ceiling but a baseline that can erode: the 8% Republican share and any potential primary opposition will emerge from a constituency frustrated by housing costs, wage stagnation, and unmet economic needs; the representative who takes 92% for granted and governs as though it is demographically inevitable will find that assumption tested when a credible challenger offers a more specific economic agenda."
