          "Lead with renter-majority and housing-cost issues: with 70.2% renters and $115,690 median income, this is a constituency of professionals who can afford to live here but face real housing-cost pressure and stability concerns; housing policy, tenant protections, and zoning reform are the material issues that determine whether constituents see their representative as delivering for them.",
          "Build deep constituent service presence in each of the district's racial and ethnic communities: the absence of a dominant demographic group (56% white, 20% Hispanic, 11% Asian, 10% Black) means that visible, responsive engagement with Hispanic, Asian, and Black constituents is both a governance obligation and essential protection against a challenger who invests in community relationships.",
          "Establish visible delivery on the issues that matter to educated professionals: transit access, school quality, public safety, and responsive local services are the baseline expectations of a 71% college-educated constituency; an incumbent who has run unopposed must demonstrate concrete results on these issues in each neighborhood to prove the seat is actively held."
