          { name: "Ignoring the Distinct Policy Needs of the Small Asian and Multiracial Constituencies", tag: "avoid", why: "While the 5.64% Asian and ~1.4% unaccounted-for populations are individually modest, in a district with multiple significant constituencies (Black, Hispanic, Asian, multiracial), the pattern of making some communities central to the candidate narrative while others become invisible signals inadequate constituent attention. Asian communities in Brooklyn face distinct economic barriers—immigrant status, credential non-recognition, healthcare language access—and multiracial constituents navigate identity-specific policy concerns that deserve representation in the legislative agenda, not absorption into broader narratives." }
