          { name: "Assuming Immigrant Communities as an Inherited Democratic Constituency", tag: "avoid", why: "With 43.4% Hispanic/Latino population and the reality of immigrant community economic vulnerability in New York City, treating immigrant voters as an automatic Democratic base is a misreading of the actual political dynamics. Immigrant communities evaluate representation on whether public services are accessible, whether education and healthcare systems serve their families, and whether the representative advocates actively for their economic security and legal status. An incumbent who takes immigrant community support for granted and does not maintain visible, sustained partnership with immigrant advocacy organizations will find that support erosion in a primary challenge scenario." }
