          { name: "Dismissing the Hispanic Community as Secondary to Black Majority Consensus", tag: "avoid", why: "While the Black majority is 67.46%, the 26.9% Hispanic population is large enough in absolute terms and concentrated enough as renters to constitute a genuine swing constituency — particularly in a primary context where turnout and mobilization matter more than general election partisan loyalty. Any incumbent or challenger who treats the Hispanic community as an afterthought within a broader minority-majority narrative, rather than engaging them on their specific material concerns around workplace rights and housing security, cedes an opportunity to activate a constituency that can shift outcomes in a heavily Democratic district where the real competition is internal, not against Republicans." }
