          "Lead with material economic results: property tax relief, healthcare affordability initiatives, utility rate advocacy, and child care cost mitigation are the issues most likely to generate genuine constituent loyalty in a working-to-middle-class suburban district where voters evaluate on practical impact rather than partisan positioning.",
          "Avoid the assumption that Democratic dominance in a New York Assembly district is automatically durable; a 25.6% college-educated, 87.81% white, homeowner-majority constituency at $66,751 income is precisely the demographic target for opposition mobilization if economic conditions worsen or incumbent responsiveness declines.",
          "Build specific relationships with the 8% Black, Hispanic, and Asian residents whose economic mobility and access concerns may become invisible in a homogeneous constituency — small populations in single-digit percentages can swing close races if they feel unserved by the incumbent."
