          "Engage the 23.3% renter constituency and 4.09% demographic gap with specific housing and cost-of-living policy rather than assuming renters are transient or minority communities are not yet core constituency — these are the demographic vectors most likely to change the district over time, and early authentic engagement builds durability.",
          "Avoid any framing that treats 64% as a safe majority; it is a strong result, but in New York's suburban realignment environment it is not insulated against credible alternative candidacy if the incumbent's district presence appears perfunctory or legislative agenda appears misaligned with community priorities."
