          "Lead with material quality-of-life delivery: property tax fairness, school funding adequacy, healthcare cost management, and responsive state services are the issues most likely to activate suburban homeowner voters in this income and age range if a credible challenger emerges.",
          "Build durable constituent relationships across the 27.3% rental population as well as the homeowner majority; renters in affluent suburban areas often perceive government as serving property owners and may swing toward a challenger who addresses housing affordability and tenant protections.",
          "Monitor demographic shifts and new development in the district; at 88.4% white with minimal diversity, changing demographics—even modest increases in Hispanic or Asian populations—could alter electoral dynamics in 2026 and beyond if not actively engaged."
