          "Build a record on education funding and property tax management specific to this district's schools and local governance — the issues that actually matter to college-educated homeowners and younger professionals in upper-middle-income suburbs. Abstract conservative positioning will not hold this seat if a Democrat runs a kitchen-table campaign on school quality and tax fairness.",
          "Engage the 26.5% renter constituency and younger professionals explicitly — this is not a district where homeowner interests can be assumed to dominate without attention. Younger renters and early-career professionals have different priorities (housing costs, student debt, reproductive freedom) than older homeowners, and ignoring this internal diversity is a tactical error.",
          "Establish consistent local presence and constituent service infrastructure — in a district where Democratic challengers are currently absent, the path to vulnerability is organizational neglect, not ideological shift. An incumbent who maintains visible engagement with schools, local government, and constituent services will be harder to challenge than one who treats the seat as secure."
