          "Engage the Black majority (41.7%) with specificity on wealth-building and anti-displacement: homeownership, small business lending, police accountability, and education funding are the material concerns of the district's dominant demographic. A representative perceived as passively managing Black constituents' interests rather than actively advancing them creates space for a challenger to mobilize this base with greater urgency.",
          "Address the 21.07% Hispanic population directly on economic mobility and wage policy: in a district where the median income is $46,168, wage floors, workplace safety, and immigration status protections are the issues that determine whether young Hispanic households can build economic security. Invisibility in a majority-Black district is a political vulnerability.",
          "Do not treat the 72% margin as a durable floor: it is a result produced by the absence of a credible alternative and constituent satisfaction with baseline service delivery. Any challenger who offers concrete policy on housing, wages, and cost of living in a 57%-renter, $46,168-median-income district can mobilize enough swing voters from the incumbent's coalition to make this competitive."
