          "Lead on housing affordability as a unifying economic message: at $67,753 income with 33.4% renters and 67% homeowners, this district lives housing costs daily. Zoning reform that enables supply, tenant protections that reduce displacement, property tax fairness, and down-payment assistance are the concrete policy answers that speak to both renters and cost-conscious homeowners.",
