          "Monitor and engage the college-educated, professional minority (35.6% college-educated) on healthcare policy, education funding, and quality-of-life issues specific to aging communities — these are the swing voters most likely to defect if an alternative candidate offers a credible platform on issues the incumbent neglects.",
          "Defend against demographic drift toward younger renters and increasing diversity: if the renter rate grows materially above 20.3% or minority population increases beyond 6-11%, the incumbent's 62% margin becomes vulnerable to a challenger who mobilizes the younger, more diverse constituency around housing affordability and economic opportunity rather than property-tax protection.",
