          "Engage the Asian-plurality constituency (44.08%) with specificity on issues that matter to immigrant and second-generation Asian families—school quality, public safety, economic mobility, and neighborhood investment—rather than assuming identity-based messaging will activate this demographically dominant group; Asian voters in high-cost urban districts are highly responsive to concrete policy delivery, not symbolic recognition.",
