          "Address the education-to-employment pipeline directly: the 37.4% college attainment suggests significant post-secondary engagement, but the $76,962 income indicates that credential does not universally translate to professional-class outcomes; apprenticeships, credential portability, wage floors, and job quality are the material concerns.",
          "Recognize that 'unopposed' is a vulnerability, not a strength: any challenger who emerges with a concrete cost-of-living message and ability to activate the 40-45% opposition that would normally appear in a contested race will find a persuadable electorate if the incumbent is not actively consolidating support on material economic concerns."
