          "Govern visibly on the specific urban quality-of-life issues that bound the district's 100% Democratic coalition together: public safety, transit reliability, school quality, and sanitation — not as talking points but as measurable improvements in constituent experience; unopposed victory creates political space to focus entirely on delivery rather than campaigning.",
