          "Recognize that 100% opposition means zero Republican competition but not zero vulnerability — the absence of organized Republican presence should signal to the incumbent that the governing agenda must remain focused on the material concerns of renters, young professionals, and service-sector workers who are not voting Republican because they see no compelling alternative, not because Democratic governance is actually delivering everything they need."
