          "Deliver on school infrastructure and youth economic mobility: with only 29.4% college attainment and a median age of 36.1, the district's working-age population depends on public schools as the primary pathway to economic mobility; visible school investment, teacher support, and college access programs are both constituent needs and political necessity in a majority-Latino district with 32% Black representation.",
          "Engage Hispanic and Black communities with specific policy attention: while the district is 52% Hispanic and 32% Black, governance cannot treat these as a unified constituency; economic mobility and healthcare access for Latino working families, and specific attention to education and wealth-building disparities in the Black community, require distinct constituent engagement and policy focus.",
          "Assume the 82% margin is durable only if performance justifies it: the supermajority reflects structural Democratic alignment, but in a low-income renter-majority district, a challenger who mobilizes around unmet tenant needs, school inadequacy, or wage stagnation can credibly contest this seat if the incumbent becomes identified with service delivery failure rather than genuine constituent advocacy."
