          { name: "Generic Democratic Positioning Without District-Specific Delivery", tag: "avoid", why: "SD-31 has a clear, measurable constituency with concrete material needs — housing stability, tenant protection, school quality, and job access. A state Senator whose legislative record is generic Democratic messaging without specific, visible wins on these district-specific issues does not meet the constituency's expectation for representation and creates vulnerability to primary challenges or local alternatives that can claim to deliver better on housing justice, school funding, or workforce development. In a district this homogeneous and economically constrained, delivery on specific constituent demands is not optional — it is the minimum threshold for holding the seat." }
