          { name: "Treating the 49% Opposition as a Monolith Rather Than a Specific Constituency", tag: "avoid", why: "In a 51-49 seat, the opposition represents nearly half the district — and at this margin, understanding specifically what concerns drive that 49% is more important than consolidating the existing 51%. Whether the opposition is concentrated among renters frustrated by housing costs, educated professionals concerned about education funding, Hispanic/Latino voters seeking economic mobility support, or some combination of these groups requires specific diagnostic work. A candidate who assumes the 51% is solid without understanding and addressing the opposition's actual concerns will find the margin collapse in the next cycle." }
