          "Lead with housing affordability and renter protection — the 29.6% renter rate in a $99k-income district is the structural fact driving Democratic underperformance; renters are experiencing cost-of-living pressure that affluence statistics mask, and they have leverage to swing close races if they perceive the incumbent as indifferent to their housing costs or quality-of-life constraints.",
          "Engage Hispanic constituency on education and economic mobility with specificity — the 20.61% Hispanic share at one-fifth of the district is large enough to be decisive in 54-46 races and will grow; Hispanic families' primary governance concerns are education quality, workforce access, and whether their children's economic mobility is plausible, and a Democratic incumbent who addresses these material concerns directly consolidates Hispanic support; one who treats Hispanic engagement as demographic maintenance loses it.",
