          "Lead with fiscal management and property tax fairness: in a district with $84,582 median income and 36% college-educated adults, constituents expect government to demonstrate efficiency and justify tax burden through transparent outcomes; a governance agenda focused on reducing waste, improving service delivery, and protecting property tax fairness speaks directly to homeowner economic security.",
          "Engage the 35.5% renter constituency specifically on housing affordability and tenant protections: one-third of the district rents rather than owns, and this population's material concerns around housing costs and lease fairness are distinct from homeowner priorities; treating renters as part of the base rather than a minority interest expands the electoral coalition.",
          "Do not treat 55% as a stable majority: a five-point margin in a high-income, college-educated, politically-aware suburban district is competitive terrain, not a comfortable hold; any candidate who consolidates the existing coalition without actively persuading swing voters and addressing opposition concerns risks losing the seat in the next cycle."
