          { name: "Assuming Unopposed Victory Reflects Durable Support", tag: "avoid", why: "A 100% result with no Democratic opposition reveals nothing about the district's actual competitive baseline or voter preference distribution. Unopposed victory is an absence of challenge, not evidence of consolidated support, and any incumbent who campaigns as though 100% in the absence of opposition translates to durable majority support will be unprepared for a resourced challenger who builds local organization and frames issues around economic opportunity or rural policy specifics." },
          { name: "Neglecting the Renter Population and Younger Adults", tag: "avoid", why: "At 29.1% renters in a predominantly homeowner district, and 42.8 median age with 27.9% college attainment, there is a constituency of younger adults and non-homeowners whose economic concerns—housing affordability, workforce mobility, student debt, agricultural employment—differ from the homeowner majority. Any legislator who defaults to homeowner-focused messaging and governance priorities while treating renters and younger adults as peripheral constituencies creates an opening for opposition that addresses these groups' material concerns directly and credibly." }
