          { name: "Educational Prestige and Credentialed Professional Narratives", tag: "avoid", why: "With only 25.8% college attainment — the lowest measure of educational stratification in any district profile — NY-SD-63 is not a constituency that automatically defers to credentialed expertise or professional class messaging. A representative who builds credibility through demonstrated effectiveness on cost-of-living issues and visible constituent service will earn trust far more effectively than one who relies on educational credentials or technocratic policy language. Avoiding messaging that privileges education-focused constituencies or implicitly positions non-college-educated workers as somehow less sophisticated or deserving of attention is essential to maintaining the breadth of the 66% coalition." }
